{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. Please stop using the appliance and unplug it if it is safe to do so. You have asked about water leaking under your Ashby tumble dryer and error code E-6876. Our help article "Water leaking underneath your Ashby tumble dryer" says you should stop the programme and switch off the dryer. If the plug, socket and surrounding area are dry, unplug it. If they are wet, switch off the circuit at the consumer unit instead, then contact Halvard Home support.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}

{"reply": "Thank you for getting in touch. You are asking how long you should wait for your Keel washing machine to cool down before you start cleaning it as part of your laundry room deep clean. Our Safety and recalls policy, section "Keel washing machine: Safe use", says you should let the Keel washing machine cool for 113 minutes before cleaning it. This duration is specified to ensure you manage the appliance safely while completing your tasks today. We hope this information helps with your cleaning schedule.

Kind regards,
The Halvard Home team"}
